<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24480" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δηναιός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δᾱναιός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ά</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>long-lived,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				5.407
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. κλέος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					16.54
				</span></i>
			; <i>long-continued,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁδοιπορίη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					14.1780
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρόνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					4.1547
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βίος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					6.39.7
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Arch.
			</span></i>): neut. as Adv., <i><span class="en">
				Man.
				3.143
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>aged,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόραι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					794
				</span></i>
			; <i>ancient,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θρόνοι</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				912
			</span></i> (and in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Eu.</u>
				846
			</span></i>(lyr.), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαναιᾶν</span> should be
			restored with Dindorf for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαμαίων,</span>
			cf. <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				105
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀοιδοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Jov.</u>
					60
				</span></i>
			; <i>worn out,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δένδρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hsch.
				</span></i>
			
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>after a long time,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. εἰσαφίκοντο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					4.645
				</span></i>
			; <i>late come, long absent,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδελφεός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>H.</u>
					4.154
				</span></i>
			: neut. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δηναιόν,</span> as
			Adv., <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				3.590
			</span></i>: so pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δηναιά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Maiist.
					8
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> personified,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Θόωσα</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δηναιή,</span>
			<u>Overspeed</u> and <i>Loitering,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Emp.
				122.3
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
